In this exam we are expected to design syntax analyzer. It parases arithmetic and conditional statements. In arithmetic we assign values to variable or
identifiers, do binary and unary arithmetic opearions. In conditional we use if and goto for opearions.

This directory contains:
Lexical file : sol.l
Syntax file : sol.y
Testcase file : input.txt

To execute it we need to do following:
1. lex <lexical_file>
2. yacc -d <syntax_file>
3. gcc lex.yy.c y.tab.c -o parser
4. ./parser < input.txt

Use this on bash:
lex sol.l
yacc -d sol.y
gcc lex.yy.c y.tab.c -o parser
./parser < input.txt

or u can do code on terminal itself after executing:
./parser


Example:
input.txt

if a < b goto L1
goto L2
L1 : t1 = a + b
goto L3
L2 : t2 = a - b
c = t2

result:
Enter code here:
Parsing successful
